      "description": "Mr. Kingston Reif, Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense for Threat Reduction and Arms Control (DASD(TRAC)), visited Richmond, Kentucky, June 7 to attend a media day regarding the impending completion of the destruction of the chemical weapons stored at the Blue Grass Army Depot (BGAD). Six local and area media outlets attended the event.\nThe media day presenters follow:\nMr. Kingston Reif, DASD(TRAC)\nMr. Michael Abaie, program executive officer, Assembled Chemical Weapons Alternatives\nDr. Candace Coyle, site project manager, Blue Grass Chemical Agent-Destruction Pilot Plant\nMr. Ron Hink, project manager, Bechtel Parsons Blue Grass\nCol. Brett Ayvazian, commander, BGAD \nLt. Col. Tyler McKee, commander, Blue Grass Chemical Activity\nJudge Executive Reagan Taylor, Madison County\n\nMr. Craig Williams, co-chair, Kentucky Chemical Demilitarization Citizens’ Advisory Commission and Chemical Destruction Community Advisory Board",
